bin/

# Working documents: implementation plans, review write-ups, red-team round
# reports, buildable specs. One committed design document per subject lives in
# .claude/design/; the process that got there does not.
#
# Ignored rather than merely untracked, and that is the point: these files were
# once removed with `git rm --cached` and a later `git add -A` in the same
# session put every one of them straight back, including a plan that had been
# deliberately untracked from the day it was written. An instruction a command
# can quietly undo is not a rule.
.claude/scratchpad/

# Agent worktrees. Same reason, one level up: a `git add -A` committed one as an
# embedded gitlink, which is a pointer to a commit the clone cannot resolve.
.claude/worktrees/
